We need to add sounds. Likely use Audio objects. Add sound loading at top: create audio elements for collect debris, asteroid hit, engine/ fuel maybe background music. Implement play when events happen.

We need to edit game.js: add const sounds = {...}. Then in checkCollisions when collecting debris play collect sound; when asteroid hit play hit sound; maybe also play engine thrust each move? Keep concise.

Add after definitions near top after stars.

Implement using new Audio('collect.wav') etc. But we have no audio files. Could use generated beep via Web Audio API? Simpler: create Audio elements with src data URLs of simple beep? Might be okay to reference placeholder URLs; the user didn't provide sounds. We'll assume they'd add files later. Use 'collect.mp3', 'hit.mp3', 'bgm.mp3'.

Implement code: const collectSound = new Audio('collect.mp3'); etc.

When player collides with debris -> collectSound.currentTime = 0; collectSound.play();

Asteroid hit -> hitSound.play();

Optionally background loop start at game start: const bgMusic = new Audio('bgm.mp3'); bgMusic.loop = true; bgMusic.play();

Add code after creating canvas and before game state.

We'll edit file.

